import GQ2.Dyadic.Instances.MpcBalancedNeutralitySpan

/-!
# The source quotient behind the neutral-C obstruction

W213 shows that the neutrality cokernel is generated by the ordinary relative `C` row.  This
file first quotients that source by the genuinely character-neutral relative classes.  The
resulting map to the W212 neutrality cokernel is still surjective.  Its kernel records exactly
the remaining cancellations of a relaxed `C` shift against the constrained coordinate span.

Thus the target cokernel is a quotient of an explicit relative-`C`-mod-neutral source.  No
injectivity or vanishing statement is asserted.
-/

namespace GQ2.Dyadic.Instances.MpcBalancedNeutralitySourceQuotient

noncomputable section

open GQ2 GQ2.Dyadic Multiplicative
open GQ2.Dyadic.MarkedCore
open GQ2.Dyadic.StageGeneric
